## Agentic pipeline

This repo uses the `agentic` plugin (https://github.com/christophe77/agentic-delivery-pipeline).
Configuration: `.agentic/pipeline.yml`.

### Cycle
1. `/agentic:epic <need>`: epic in Monday (human approval)
2. `/agentic:tickets <epic id>`: tickets as vertical slices (human approval)
3. `/agentic:implement <ticket id>`: branch from `staging`, code, tests, PR to `staging`
4. On the PR (CI): AI review + deploy to `dev` and browser QA on dev; `/agentic:review <PR>` locally
5. Merge into `staging`: **human**
6. Automatic staging deployment, then browser QA on staging (CI)
7. `/agentic:release prepare`: promotion PR `staging` -> `main`; merge (**human**), then production approval (**human**)
8. Automatic production deployment, then read-only smoke QA on production (CI)
9. `/agentic:release close`: Monday tickets moved to Done

### Conventions
- Branches: `{type}/{item_id}-{slug}` (e.g. `feat/1234567890-export-csv`)
- Conventional commits, with a `Monday: #<item_id>` footer
- One PR = one ticket
- Definition of done: acceptance criteria tested, lint/tests/build green, review with no blocker, QA passed on dev and staging

